610?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">AI is a hot topic at this year's Frankfurt Book Fair. An international literary scandal raises questions about machine-generated texts.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>US imposes sanctions aiming to 'dismantle' International Criminal Court</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b01dbaf0573d3339509caa012517132e2893990b27d6976460e1000905cd78b3</id><updated>2026-10-09T15:23:35Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T14:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-imposes-sanctions-aiming-to-dismantle-international-criminal-court/a-79618577--3c15e900b5b5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-imposes-sanctions-aiming-to-dismantle-international-criminal-court/a-79618577?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The US has announced new sanctions on the International Criminal Court. It's the latest in a series of steps by the Donald Trump administration as it seeks to "dismantle" the intergovernmental organization.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Saudi coalition vows 'firm' response after airport attack kills 3</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:59b9bdde926470c59b55c8428bc408c7cf9426df9bc514d41163e8d0c05657be</id><updated>2026-10-09T15:23:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T14:01:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/saudi-coalition-vows-firm-response-after-airport-attack-kills-3/a-79615437--46e08f9efd21.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/saudi-coalition-vows-firm-response-after-airport-attack-kills-3/a-79615437?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Saudi Arabia and its allied forces in Yemen vowed a "firm response" to Houthi attacks that target civilians. The kingdom's authorities said three Saudi nationals were killed in Thursday's attack on Riyadh airport.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Is China seeking to restrict Taiwan's cultural presence?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4c85ca87514ba109456523c61f76ca175a0fcd7063ee7019ab26470adc8949cf</id><updated>2026-10-09T15:23:41Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T13:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/is-china-seeking-to-restrict-taiwan-s-cultural-presence/a-79610947--71784c91bb83.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/is-china-seeking-to-restrict-taiwan-s-cultural-presence/a-79610947?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">From coffee competitions to literature awards, Beijing appears to be working to limit Taiwan's international cultural and political impact.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Art for freedom: Maria Kalesnikava in Bonn</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d5e5b250e2727fbe3a121455f0f5dcfb808f2e93258ee75f219bf24284fea482</id><updated>2026-10-09T15:23:44Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T13:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/art-for-freedom-maria-kalesnikava-in-bonn/a-79612009--0f2314a86e67.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/art-for-freedom-maria-kalesnikava-in-bonn/a-79612009?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Belarusian musician and civil rights activist Maria Kalesnikava held the keynote speech on the importance of art at the 2026 Beethovenfest in Bonn. She also visited DW.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Poland: Lifeline for Ukrainian refugees confronts donor fatigue and online abuse as anti-Ukrainian sentiment grows</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:28b812a62b076f88162b5a9de8f574b296dd1e18022c2edabd049846d2856aff</id><updated>2026-10-09T15:23:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T12:50:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/poland-lifeline-for-ukrainian-refugees-confronts-donor-fatigue-and-online-abuse-as-anti-ukrainian-se/a-79613292--19cba8c4d4f1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/poland-lifeline-for-ukrainian-refugees-confronts-donor-fatigue-and-online-abuse-as-anti-ukrainian-sentiment-grows/a-79613292?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A Ukrainian woman who fled the war in her country built a lifeline for refugees in Poland. Now her organization faces donor fatigue, funding cuts and rising hostility as support for Ukrainians in Poland wanes.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>India's 'cockroaches' vs Election Commission: What you need to know ahead of CJP's October 10 protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ce04519852309bc08ef62e1d1ce883c65bfb6f40c9c409d209f2a849ca7f0bfe</id><updated>2026-10-09T15:23:50Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T12:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-s-cockroaches-vs-election-commission-what-you-need-to-know-ahead-of-cjp-s-october-10-protests/a-79608760--fa9a4a7bb711.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-s-cockroaches-vs-election-commission-what-you-need-to-know-ahead-of-cjp-s-october-10-protests/a-79608760?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Indian capital New Delhi has been turned into a fortress with train and metro cancelations, barricades and heavy police presence ahead of Saturday's planned protests against the chief of India's electoral body.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Hurricane Isaias intensifies en route to US Gulf Coast</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:427b9bba665159da52564c1078f376e5bb9bf18f99f41d3f3c4d88ec22a60427</id><updated>2026-10-09T15:23:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T11:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/hurricane-isaias-intensifies-en-route-to-us-gulf-coast/a-79612756--4e23d2ef7c5c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/hurricane-isaias-intensifies-en-route-to-us-gulf-coast/a-79612756?maca=en-rss-en-top-10